From fd045e408e6b65e8748ca6f1f7601e70980d3be7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lynx Authors <noreply@lynxjs.org>
Date: Tue, 25 Aug 2026 22:13:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [BugFix] Fix Linux DNS resolution and 304 handling

Two independent defects, both found while bringing up a Linux desktop
host.

1. DNS resolution fails intermittently under concurrency (glibc only).

On glibc, a non-zero connection timeout selects the getaddrinfo_a path.
gai_suspend() returns EAI_ALLDONE when the lookup completed before the
wait began, which happens routinely once a resolver thread is warm and
constantly when requests overlap. That return was treated as a failure,
discarding an address that had already resolved successfully and leaking
its addrinfo, so requests failed with 'Could not establish connection'
without a syscall ever reaching the network.

Measured against a local server, same machine, before and after:

  concurrency  1    2      4      8      16
  before       0%   5.0%   7.5%   6.7%   -
  after        0%   0%     0%     0%     0%

This branch is inside '#elif defined(_GNU_SOURCE) && defined(__GLIBC__)',
so no other platform is affected.

2. 304 Not Modified is followed as a redirect.

304 is in the 3xx range but is not a redirect and carries no Location, so
redirect() failed and the caller saw an opaque transport error instead of
the response:

  before:  error=Unknown  status=-1
  after:   error=Success  status=304

This one is not platform-scoped, so it is worth being explicit about why
it is safe. The library was already internally inconsistent: the
equivalent test in process_request() excludes 304 when deciding whether a
response is a redirect, while the test in send_() did not. This change
makes the two agree with each other. Nothing can depend on the previous
behaviour, because the previous behaviour produced no status, no headers
and no body -- only Error::Unknown.
---
 httplib.cc | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/httplib.cc b/httplib.cc
index b78bb4f..d8d0bf9 100644
--- a/httplib.cc
+++ b/httplib.cc
@@ -1676,6 +1676,16 @@ int getaddrinfo_with_timeout(const char *node, const char *service,
       if (request.ar_result) { freeaddrinfo(request.ar_result); }
       return gai_result;
     }
+  } else if (wait_result == EAI_ALLDONE) {
+    // The lookup completed before gai_suspend() began waiting. That is a
+    // success, not a failure: treat it exactly like wait_result == 0.
+    int gai_result = gai_error(&request);
+    if (gai_result == 0) {
+      *res = request.ar_result;
+      return 0;
+    }
+    if (request.ar_result) { freeaddrinfo(request.ar_result); }
+    return gai_result;
   } else if (wait_result == EAI_AGAIN) {
     // Timeout occurred, cancel the request
     gai_cancel(&request);
@@ -4768,7 +4778,10 @@ bool ClientImpl::handle_request(Stream &strm, Request &req,
     close_socket(socket_);
   }
 
-  if (300 < res.status && res.status < 400 && follow_location_) {
+  // 304 is in the 3xx range but is not a redirect and carries no Location,
+  // so following it turns a valid conditional response into an error.
+  if (300 < res.status && res.status < 400 &&
+      res.status != StatusCode::NotModified_304 && follow_location_) {
     req = req_save;
     ret = redirect(req, res, error);
   }
